# Purpose: keep Terraform working files and state out of Git.
# State lives in the remote S3 backend (see aws/backend.tf); local state and provider caches are never committed.
#
# Note: *.tfvars files are NOT ignored on purpose. The example files under aws/envs/ contain no secrets
# (only sizes, CIDRs, public SSH keys and example.com names). Secrets are never put in tfvars: they are
# set out of band in AWS Secrets Manager, or passed to CI as TF_VAR_* environment variables.
# Local overrides that might contain secrets use the *.auto.tfvars / *.local.tfvars names below.

**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.local.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
